tests:
  unit: { count: 51, covers: "The shell's scenario (scenario.rs, run with cargo test --features scenario in ui/src-tauri: 52 there, 36 without the feature): a fresh scenario is an untrusted machine with no proxy that refuses every confirm; a patch moves only the fields it names and one naming an unknown field is refused; each trust and proxy reading goes through the shell's own trust_word and read_proxy, an unreadable proxy reaching the classifier as today's absence; a set-up that succeeds trusts and routes through the address asked for; a cancelled prompt reads as refused through the real command_failed; a failed tool keeps its words and changes nothing; a silent failure takes the real command's no-detail sentence; an unset turns the proxy off; the launch's opening patch from the environment; each host becomes a user agent the frontend reads as that host, and an unknown host is refused. The harness front (front.rs): the scripted reach answers unarmed and armed in the core's shape on the core's ports, refuses an address the script does not hold, serialises the fields the app reads, a down front drops the connection rather than answering, an up front answers /reach itself. The command (walkthrough.rs): the plan judge accepts a full grid naming every finding and refuses a finding no chapter names, one the review lacks, a missing host x platform reel, duplicate ids and an empty expectation; a run's verdict is green only when every scripted chapter was framed on disk or skipped with a reason, and red with a sentence for a run that stopped early, left no manifest, recorded a missing frame, or filmed out of order; the caption, SRT and WebVTT timings, a caption that cannot end its cue, the concat list repeating its last frame, the ffmpeg argv, and the index escaping captions with one tick-box per chapter. ui.rs: walkthrough takes no arguments and is in the usage text, and the no-partial-text-selector guard now reads ui/e2e/walkthrough too; its existing tests still run beside them." }
  integration: { count: 4, covers: "The WU contract at the assembler, over a fixture output tree of real PNG frames and run manifests with the stitch step injected: every reel that filmed gets a video, a caption track and a place in the index, its launches' frames in script order and one tick-box per chapter including skips; a chapter whose anchor never painted turns the assembly red naming the reel, launch and chapter, and its reel gets no video while the index says why; a launch that never ran is a reel that did not film; a stitch that fails is red for its reel." }
  e2e: { waived: "The walkthrough run is this WU's deliverable and was run as its evidence: two full cargo xtask ui walkthrough runs through the real Tauri window against a real ephemeral core, the first red on the one chapter the script got wrong (linux-ios-sim/walk stopped before chapter 3, no video written), the second green with 24 reels, 144 chapters, 24 videos and the index. The epic's e2e is W6's, per the epic plan." }
